# build output
build/
*.o
*.d
*.elf
*.img
*.lst
*.map
*.hex

# fetched sources and toolchain-side build tree
#
# No trailing slash, and that is deliberate: `third_party/` does not match a
# SYMLINK called third_party, because a symlink is not a directory to git.  In
# the clean clone of .80 the two symlinks to the old tree showed up as untracked
# and would have gone into the commit as links to /home/<someone>/... .  Without
# the slash the pattern matches the name whether it is a directory, a file or a
# link.
third_party
sdcard

# the Arm toolchain, unpacked by scripts/setup.sh.  It lives here on purpose
# (self-contained tree), so it is not something a clone has to install.
opt

# python bytecode from the check generators
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# editor noise
*~
.vscode/

# Internal working notes and the engineering log.  They are kept out of the
# published repository on purpose: they are a diary, not documentation, and the
# two READMEs are written for readers who are not the person writing this.
docs/
AGENTS.md
NOTAS-TECNICAS.md

# Working scripts that live OUTSIDE the tree (in ~/entrega/).  They are listed
# here because one of them -- crear-mensaje-commit.sh -- was committed into the
# root of the published repo in v0.78 by a `git add -A` (see AGENTS.md 17.21 and
# entrega/REVISION-REPO-0.78.md).  It was removed again in 444e70d ("Remove a
# local helper script that should never have been committed"), but .gitignore
# does not un-track anything by itself: these two lines are what keeps it out
# next time, whatever happens to the local .git.
crear-mensaje-commit.sh
hacer-imagen.sh
